		summary = '**Robert Burns** (25 January 1759 – 21 July 1796), also known familiarly as **Rabbie Burns**, was a Scottish poet and lyricist. He is widely regarded as the national poet of [[Scotland]] and is celebrated worldwide. He is the best known of the poets who have written in the [[Scots language]], although much of his writing is in a "light Scots dialect" of English, accessible to an audience beyond Scotland. He also wrote in standard English, and in these writings his political or civil commentary is often at its bluntest.',
